Voice Classification with Multiple Linear Regression

Download Audio_Speech_Actors_01-24_16k.zip here: https://zenodo.org/records/11063852

Create a folder named dataset next to main.cpp and extract the ZIP into it. The Actor_01 to Actor_24 folders should be inside dataset/Audio_Speech_Actors_01-24_16k/.

Open PowerShell in the project folder. You need g++ with C++17 support. Run these two commands.

g++ -std=c++17 -O2 main.cpp -o voice.exe
.\voice.exe

The program uses central finite differences and gradient descent to train on actors 01 to 16, then tests on actors 17 to 24. It got 311 of 458 predictions correct (67.90%). It skipped 22 test recordings without a usable pitch estimate.

At the last prompt, enter the path to a 16 kHz, 16-bit PCM WAV file to classify it, or press Enter to quit.
